WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.890
It's game show week, Ross.

2
00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.910
And to celebrate we're gamifying the news.

3
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.530
Are you ready?
Oh, I'm ready.

4
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:08.388
It's Pop Culture Showdown!
Yes!

5
00:00:08.388 --> 00:00:10.971
(upbeat music)

6
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.280
And we're the contestants today.

7
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.130
Oh, and it is on, Drew.
I'm so excited.

8
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.470
We're gonna play with each other.

9
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.340
And every game show needs a host.

10
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.210
And I know a host who's the most qualified

11
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.370
when it comes to pop culture, or anything else in the biz.

12
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.190
He's the host of "Entertainment Tonight",

13
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.020
now in its 40th season.

14
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.310
Please welcome our friend, Kevin Frazier!

15
00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:35.210
Hi Kevin!

16
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.650
Drew, how are you?

17
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.690
Oh Kevin, I love how...
Hey Ross.

18
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.076
Hi, I love you.

19
00:00:42.076 --> 00:00:43.690
(Ross giggles)

20
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.227
This makes me so happy, Kevin, thank you.

21
00:00:46.227 --> 00:00:50.160
I am so excited to be a game show host right now, Drew.

22
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.520
All right, well before we play,

23
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.030
you brought us an amazing clip from the "ET" archives.

24
00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.030
Take it away, Kevin.

25
00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:57.100
Tell us who it is.

26
00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.640
Yeah, Bob Barker, because the "Price is Right"

27
00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.500
is the longest running game show on TV.

28
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.770
And Bob hosted it for almost 35 years,

29
00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.940
starting all the way back in 1972.

30
00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.660
He is the greatest of all time,

31
00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:10.030
the GOAT is we like to say.

32
00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.960
And when the American TV icon sat down with "ET",

33
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.780
back in 1986, he talked about why games

34
00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.340
and game shows have such staying power.

35
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.173
Check this out.

36
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.840
Well, I believe that Americans are game oriented.

37
00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.840
We play games at home as children, preschool children.

38
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.120
Families play games together.

39
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.520
They play games as they travel

40
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.160
in automobiles or on airplanes.

41
00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.900
And we play games on social occasions.

42
00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:42.700
And games were popular on radio many years ago.

43
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:45.943
And it was only a natural transition to television.

44
00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:48.250
Okay.
I love him.

45
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:49.083
We love games!

46
00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:50.260
That's what he told us.

47
00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.360
And because we love games we're gonna play.

48
00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.840
You both love pop culture.

49
00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.510
And we're about to put that to the test, all right.

50
00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.490
I get a little competitive, Kevin.

51
00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.370
We're going to confer with each other

52
00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.640
and then tell Kevin the answer, right?

53
00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.170
Okay, understood.
Okay, perfect, got it.

54
00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.290
Here's the first question.

55
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.380
Warner Brothers just announced "Wonka",

56
